      },
      "lineNbr": 107,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-09-28T09:57:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we need some consistency here in tense. Right now there are three different conventions in this file :\n\n- A noun describing what is concerned (e.g. onInterfaceDnsServerEvent)\n- A present tense verb (e.g. onInterfaceRemoveEvent, onRouteChangeEvent)\n- A past tense verb (e.g. onInterfaceChangedEvent)\n\nI think either convention is fine, but we should have consistency. Looking only at this file, because this is events sent by netd to listeners to warn them that something did happen, I would favor the past tense, but it also depends on what other aidl files in the vicinity does – a quick look at the directory, especially INetworkManagementEventObserver also tends to advocate for past tenses.\n\nWhat do you think ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 107,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 107,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "9e23ce88d162c943c470f66c616aeb4973e7c308",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
